###############Docker volume container##############

Q1. Docker Volume Persistence
Volumes are the preferred mechanism for persisting data generated by and used by Docker containers.

Create the volume:
docker volume create data_vol

Run the first container:
docker run -it --name helper_cont -v data_vol:/data alpine sh

Inside the container, create a file:
echo "Persistence test" > /data/testfile.txt && exit

Remove the container:
docker rm helper_cont

Run a new container with the same volume:
docker run -it --name verifier_cont -v data_vol:/data alpine cat /data/testfile.txt
(The output should display "Persistence test")
