Q9. Dockerfile – C Application
Create the C source file (hello.c):

C
#include <stdio.h>

int main() {
    printf("Hello from a C program running in Docker!\n");
    return 0;
}
Create the Dockerfile:

We use gcc as the base image because it comes pre-installed with the tools needed to compile C code.

Dockerfile
# Use an image that has GCC installed
FROM gcc:latest

# Set the working directory inside the container
WORKDIR /usr/src/app

# Copy the C file into the container
COPY hello.c .

# Compile the C program
RUN gcc -o my_c_app hello.c

# Run the compiled binary
CMD ["./my_c_app"]
Build the Image:
Run this command in your terminal (ensure you are in the folder containing the files):
docker build -t c-app .

Run the Container:
docker run c-app

